        {
          "id": 2009320250,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Asciidoctor-pdf 1.6.x doesn't automatically add the default font path, you have to specify it in addition to the extra font path. But in 1.6.x the only way to separate multiple font paths is `;` on Windows and `:` on UN*X. In 2.0.x and later it seems that the default (internal to the Ruby gem) path is always searched (if you specify a font name from the default selection.) It's also possible to use `,` as a separator on all platforms, which is especially nice because semicolon has some terrible escaping and quoting rules with both CMake and Windows/MSVC.\n\nAs a last resort, it's possible to put the default fallback fonts in our directory as well.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
